 "show": "Fred again.. & Baby Keem - leavemealone",
 "about": "Bars of the analysis grid: bar b starts at 0.416 + 1.379 b seconds, 162 bars at 174 bpm. The grid's bar line sits one beat before the music's downbeat -- the bass lands on beat two of every grid bar and the snare on grid beats one and three -- so every mark is written at b.25, the beat the bass actually lands on. The track is a 174 two-step that keeps stopping dead. The ears play the drums: the kick on the rims on 1 and the and of 3, the snare up the tubes on 2 and 4. Eight warm sparks looping every bar on the face are the chopped vocal, and they come back whenever it does. Every stop empties the helmet to the vocal chop traded beat by beat between the left half + ear 1 and the right half + ear 2, and one cold light on its own. Room is the intimate parts, heat the hooks, pushing out in rings from the middle of the face. In the hooks the left half + ear 1 call on 1 and the right half + ear 2 answer on 3; in the verse ear 1 keeps the snare and ear 2 carries the voice. The title crosses the face once, alone, in the breakdown. White once, on the last drop at 140.25. Shell layers are written to sit inside the shell's 300 mA, so the guard is not the one choreographing.",
